# scripts/cron_beats.manifest - expected beat cadence of the box crons (package K6, 2026-11-03). One job per line: <job> <interval_minutes> <critical 0|1>.
# Read by ops/cron_beats_check.py (08:00 heartbeat line). A job is STALE when its beat (state/beats/<job>, written by ops/cron_beat.sh) is older than interval x3.
# Derived from the box's LIVE crontab (2026-11-03) with `python3 ops/cron_beats_check.py --derive <crontab text>`: interval = longest gap between two runs; the job name is the
# script basename (suffixed with the next plain word / a counter when one script has several cron lines: ovn_work_supply_<repo>, ovn_notify_update, branch_hygiene_1..4).
# branch_hygiene_1 = dev repos hourly, _2 = billwatch+website /3h, _3 = claude/feature pass dev repos, _4 = claude/feature pass prod repos.
# critical=1: a safety net whose silence must be noticed first (hygiene, reconcile, pause/lock guards, GPU autoswap, autofix, notifier, hourly backup, queue health). Only jobs that
# the proposed '#OFF#' lines in scripts/cron.txt can wrap are listed (compound lines such as spec_gate / mutation scan are wrapped by hand and added here afterwards).
# Only jobs wrapped on an ACTIVE crontab line are judged (the rest read 'unwrapped'); a wrapped job with no beat is 'pending' for interval x3 after the checker first saw it wrapped, then 'never'.
